cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these analyses, please cite both the software and the article."
title: "identity-retention: the pre-registered pipeline for the identity-retention fraction in paired tumor-adjacent expression contrasts, with the retentionfrac package"
abstract: >-
  A single-function Python package and the complete pre-registered analysis
  pipeline behind it. The identity-retention fraction is the intercept of the
  paired-difference regression of a signature on a tissue-identity score built
  from disjoint genes, expressed as a share of the unadjusted paired shift. The
  function checks the identity premise and the stability of the ratio before it
  returns a value, and refuses to return one when either fails.
